      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T17:36:25Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "Ack, WRT the VDO macro being poorly factored. It should take more parameters and probably have structured and unstructured versions with more expressive names.\n\nIf a macro (or function) had those things, I think it would have preferable semantics to setting the fields individually:\n1) Assigning to the entire VDO would make it more obvious that the object was being completely initialized, whereas leaving various fields in their previous states (including reserved fields that technically should be zeroed) prompts some explanation.\n2) Encapsulating the construction of individual fields via, e.g. VDO_CMDT(), would factor it out of this function, which I believe is an appropriate level of abstraction in the PE.\n\nSince, as you point out, the current macro is not fully suited to these benefits, and making it better would be out of scope, I will downgrade this to a nit.",
      "parentUuid": "deedad98_91e4024c",
